    <text>
        <body>
            <div type="edition">
            <ab>Transcription goes here</ab></div>
            
            <div type="translation">
            <p></p></div>

            <div type="commentary">
            <p>Cornell digital collection: This is a cast of a fragment of a cuneiform inscription
                    in Old Persian from the Apadana at Persepolis housed in the British Museum. It
                    includes four lines of text written horizontally, with each line separated by a
                    thin inscribed line. The top of a fifth line of writing is also preserved along
                    the bottom of the block. Sculpted borders at the top and right edges indicate
                    that it is from the top right corner of a larger inscription. The inscription
                    originally ran for thirty lines and was a dedication by Xerxes I to Ahuramazda
                    intended to glorify both the god and the king and also to legitimate the king's
                    rule.</p></div>
            

            <div type="bibliography"> <xi:include href="http://library.brown.edu/usep_data/resources/titles.xml"> <xi:fallback> <p>US Ep bibliography</p> </xi:fallback> </xi:include> </div>

